<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tô Lâm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1957">1957</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tô Lâm is a Vietnamese politician and career police officer who became general secretary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-vietnam">Communist Party of Vietnam</a> in August 2024, after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-phu-trong">Nguyen Phu Trong</a>. As minister of public security from 2016 to 2024 he directed much of the party's anti-corruption campaign, and he briefly served as state president in 2024 before taking the party leadership.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Van Linh (1986–1991), the architect of the reform era, Do Muoi, Le Kha Phieu, Nong Duc Manh and Nguyen Phu Trong (2011–2024), who led a sweeping anti-corruption campaign known as the ‘blazing furnace’ that forced out senior officials, including two state presidents; <b>To Lam</b> succeeded him in 2024.</blockquote><a href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Socialist Republic of Vietnam · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
